<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#05060a">
<title>The Founder's File</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ url_for('static', filename='style.css') }}">
</head>
<body>

<div class="bg-field" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="glow"></div>
</div>

<!-- ==================== LANDING PAGE ==================== -->
<div id="landingPage" class="landing-page">
  <button class="ghost landing-login-btn" id="landingLoginBtn" type="button">Log in</button>
  <div class="landing-inner">
    <h1 class="landing-title">The Founder's File</h1>
    <p class="landing-tagline">Turn a raw business idea into a real case file — a sentiment read, a business model, a tax organizer, and a hands-on simulator, grounded in real cited sources instead of generic advice.</p>

    <div class="landing-cta-row">
      <button class="primary landing-cta" id="landingGetStarted1"><span>Get started</span></button>
    </div>

    <div class="landing-example">
      <div class="landing-example-label">What you'll see — an example rating</div>
      <div class="landing-example-card">
        <div class="landing-score">78<span>/100</span></div>
        <div class="landing-example-text">
          <div class="landing-example-verdict">Worth a pilot</div>
          <p>A subscription hot sauce box aimed at home cooks who already buy specialty ingredients online has a real, if crowded, market — differentiation and retention are the open questions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-example-bars">
        <div class="landing-example-bar-row"><span>Money in</span><div class="landing-example-bar-track"><div class="landing-example-bar in" style="width:70%"></div></div></div>
        <div class="landing-example-bar-row"><span>Money out</span><div class="landing-example-bar-track"><div class="landing-example-bar out" style="width:45%"></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="landing-example">
      <div class="landing-example-label">The Simulator — capital vs. personal income, projected out</div>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 800 220" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" class="landing-sim-chart">
        <line x1="60" y1="20" x2="60" y2="190" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.12)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <line x1="60" y1="190" x2="770" y2="190" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.12)" stroke-width="1"/>
        <path d="M 60 160 L 200 140 L 340 110 L 480 80 L 620 50 L 770 25" fill="none" stroke="#5b8def" stroke-width="3"/>
        <path d="M 60 185 L 200 178 L 340 165 L 480 148 L 620 128 L 770 105" fill="none" stroke="#3ecf8e" stroke-width="3"/>
      </svg>
      <div class="landing-sim-legend">
        <span class="landing-sim-legend-item"><i class="sim-swatch" style="background:#5b8def"></i> Business capital</span>
        <span class="landing-sim-legend-item"><i class="sim-swatch" style="background:#3ecf8e"></i> Owner personal income</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="landing-features">
      <div class="landing-feature"><h3>Should I do this?</h3><p>A grounded, evidence-based read on your idea's odds — not a generic pep talk.</p></div>
      <div class="landing-feature"><h3>The business model</h3><p>Customer, revenue model, and a clear picture of what money comes in vs. goes out.</p></div>
      <div class="landing-feature"><h3>Tax &amp; finance</h3><p>A projected Schedule C, tax strategies, and a recommendation on how to register your business.</p></div>
      <div class="landing-feature"><h3>Simulator</h3><p>Pure math, no AI — play with capital, revenue streams, and payout choices yourself.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="landing-cta-row">
      <button class="primary landing-cta" id="landingGetStarted2"><span>Get started</span></button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ==================== SIGN-IN PAGE ==================== -->
<div id="authPage" class="auth-page" style="display:none;">
  <div class="auth-page-inner">
    <h2 id="authPageTitle">Create your account</h2>
    <p class="auth-page-sub">Every case file is tied to your account, so your work is there when you come back.</p>

    <a class="social-btn google" id="googleLoginBtn" href="/auth/google/login" style="display:none;">
      <span class="social-icon">G</span> Continue with Google
    </a>
    <div class="or-divider"><span>or</span></div>

    <div class="field">
      <label for="authEmail">Email</label>
      <input type="text" id="authEmail" placeholder="you@example.com" autocomplete="email" />
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="authPassword">Password</label>
      <input type="password" id="authPassword" placeholder="At least 8 characters" autocomplete="current-password" />
    </div>
    <div class="auth-error" id="authError" style="display:none;"></div>
    <button class="primary" id="authSubmit" style="width:100%;"><span>Create account</span></button>

    <p class="auth-page-switch">
      <span id="authSwitchToLogin">Already have an account? <a href="#" id="switchToLoginLink">Log in</a></span>
      <span id="authSwitchToSignup" style="display:none;">Need an account? <a href="#" id="switchToSignupLink">Create one</a></span>
    </p>
    <button class="ghost auth-back-btn" id="authBackToLanding" type="button">&larr; Back</button>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ==================== APP SHELL ==================== -->
<div id="appShell" class="app-shell" style="display:none;">

  <!-- LEFT SIDEBAR: step navigation, sticky -->
  <nav class="side-nav" id="sideNav">
    <div class="side-nav-title">The Founder's File</div>
    <button class="side-nav-item active" data-round="0" id="navStep0">
      <span class="side-nav-num"></span><span class="side-nav-label">The idea</span>
    </button>
    <div class="side-nav-divider"></div>
    <button class="side-nav-item locked" data-round="1" id="navStep1" disabled>
      <span class="side-nav-num" id="status1"></span><span class="side-nav-label">Should I do this?</span>
    </button>
    <button class="side-nav-item locked" data-round="2" id="navStep2" disabled>
      <span class="side-nav-num" id="status2"></span><span class="side-nav-label">Business model &amp; Simulator</span>
    </button>
    <button class="side-nav-item locked" data-round="3" id="navStep3" disabled>
      <span class="side-nav-num" id="status3"></span><span class="side-nav-label">Tax &amp; finance</span>
    </button>
    <div class="side-nav-divider"></div>
    <button class="side-nav-item" data-round="5" id="navStep5">
      <span class="side-nav-num"></span><span class="side-nav-label">Learn</span>
    </button>
  </nav>

  <!-- MAIN CONTENT -->
  <main class="main-col">

    <!-- STEP 0: THE IDEA (required intake, gates everything else) -->
    <div class="case-page round-page" id="round0">
      <div class="round-label">The idea</div>
      <h2>Tell us about the venture</h2>
      <p class="dek">This is the one thing we need before anything else — your budget and location directly shape the rating and every round after it.</p>

      <div class="field">
        <label for="ideaName">Case / idea name</label>
        <input type="text" id="ideaName" placeholder="Name this venture (e.g. 'Riverside Coffee Cart')" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="ideaBudget">Starting budget</label>
        <input type="text" id="ideaBudget" placeholder="e.g. $8,000 or 'under $2,000'" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="ideaLocation">Business location</label>
        <input type="text" id="ideaLocation" placeholder="e.g. Austin, TX" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="ideaPrompt">Describe the idea</label>
        <textarea id="ideaPrompt" placeholder="e.g. A subscription box that sends hot sauce from a different small producer every month, aimed at home cooks who already buy specialty ingredients online."></textarea>
        <div class="hint">Be specific about the product, who buys it, and where — a sharper prompt gets a sharper read.</div>
      </div>
      <button class="primary" id="runAnalysis"><span>Rate this idea</span></button>

      <div id="analysisLoading" style="display:none;"></div>
      <div id="analysisResult"></div>
      <div class="empty-note" id="analysisDoneNote" style="display:none;margin-top:16px;">Rated — see the result on the <strong>Should I do this?</strong> tab on the left.</div>
    </div>

    <!-- ROUND 1 (kept for internal state/id compatibility; content now mirrors round0's result) -->
    <div class="case-page round-page" id="round1" style="display:none;">
      <div class="round-label">Round 1 — Sentiment read</div>
      <h2>Should I make this a business?</h2>
      <p class="dek">The read on your idea, based on what you told us on the previous step.</p>
      <div id="round1Result"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- ROUND 2 + SIMULATOR (merged: two sections stacked) -->
    <div class="case-page round-page" id="round2" style="display:none;">
      <div class="round-label">Round 2 — Business model &amp; Simulator</div>
      <h2>How the money moves</h2>
      <p class="dek">Pulled from your idea where possible. Fill in the gaps, and Claude will sketch a full one-page model — revenue lines, customer, and what it costs to start.</p>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="r2notes">Anything to add or correct before Claude drafts the model?</label>
        <textarea id="r2notes" placeholder="Optional — e.g. 'I want to start online-only, no storefront.'"></textarea>
      </div>
      <button class="primary" id="runModel"><span>Draft the business model</span></button>
      <div id="modelLoading" style="display:none;"></div>
      <div id="modelResult"></div>

      <div class="section-divider" style="margin:34px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"></div>

      <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin:18px 0 6px;">Play with the numbers yourself</h3>
      <p class="dek">Pure math, no AI involved. Set your starting capital, add revenue streams, and choose per-stream whether it reinvests into the business or pays out to you personally — then watch the two lines over time.</p>

      <details style="margin-bottom:20px;padding:12px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:6px;">
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink-soft);">Calculation methodology &amp; assumptions</summary>
        <ul style="margin:12px 0 0 20px;font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.6;">
          <li><strong>Revenue:</strong> User-entered monthly amount × number of months = annual projection</li>
          <li><strong>Reinvestment vs. Payout:</strong> Toggle per stream determines whether revenue increases business capital or owner personal income</li>
          <li><strong>Tax impact:</strong> No tax is deducted — reference Round 3 Schedule C projections for tax implications</li>
          <li><strong>Accuracy:</strong> This is illustrative only — consult a CPA or financial advisor for real business planning</li>
        </ul>
      </details>

      <div class="sim-controls">
        <div class="field sim-field-inline">
          <label for="simInitialInvestment">Initial investment ($)</label>
          <input type="number" id="simInitialInvestment" value="10000" min="0" step="500" />
        </div>
        <div class="field sim-field-inline">
          <label for="simMonths">Months to simulate</label>
          <input type="number" id="simMonths" value="24" min="1" max="120" step="1" />
        </div>
        <button class="primary" id="simStartBtn" type="button"><span>Start / update simulation</span></button>
        <button class="ghost" id="simImportBtn" type="button">Import from above</button>
      </div>

      <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:20px 0 10px;">Money flow — click a stream to highlight it</h3>
      <div class="sim-flow-wrap">
        <svg id="simFlowDiagram" viewBox="0 0 800 320" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"></svg>
      </div>

      <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:20px 0 10px;">Revenue streams — edit or add as many as you want</h3>
      <div id="simStreams" class="sim-streams"></div>
      <button class="ghost" id="simAddStreamBtn" type="button">+ Add revenue stream</button>

      <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:22px 0 10px;">Capital vs. personal income over time</h3>
      <div class="sim-chart-wrap">
        <div class="sim-legend">
          <span class="sim-legend-item"><i class="sim-swatch sim-swatch-capital"></i> Business capital</span>
          <span class="sim-legend-item"><i class="sim-swatch sim-swatch-income"></i> Owner personal income (cumulative)</span>
        </div>
        <svg id="simChart" viewBox="0 0 800 300" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"></svg>
      </div>
      <div id="simSummary" class="sim-summary"></div>

      <h3 style="font-size:14px;margin:22px 0 10px;">Projected value per revenue stream</h3>
      <div class="sim-chart-wrap">
        <div class="sim-legend" id="simStreamLegend"></div>
        <svg id="simStreamChart" viewBox="0 0 800 260" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"></svg>
      </div>

      <div class="section-divider" style="margin:34px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"></div>

      <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin:0 0 6px;">Cushion fund</h3>
      <p class="dek">How much cash you personally have set aside before this business needs to make you money.</p>

      <div class="field">
        <label for="cushionFundAmount">Cushion fund ($)</label>
        <input type="number" id="cushionFundAmount" value="" min="0" step="100" placeholder="e.g. 5000" />
        <div class="hint">Don't know your number? <button type="button" id="cushionWizardOpenBtn" style="background:none;border:none;color:#5b8def;cursor:pointer;padding:0;font-size:inherit;text-decoration:underline;">Walk me through it</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ROUND 3 -->
    <div class="case-page round-page" id="round3" style="display:none;">
      <div class="round-label">Round 3 — Tax &amp; finance</div>
      <h2>Schedule C &amp; keeping more of it</h2>
      <p class="dek">Optional. Claude maps your model to the deduction categories a sole proprietor actually files under, flags what needs a real accountant, recommends how to register your business, and points to firms that work with small businesses.</p>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="r3expenses">Business expenses (optional)</label>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
          <button class="ghost" id="mockExtensionBtn" type="button" style="padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 13px;">Autofill sample expenses</button>
          <button class="ghost" id="useSimInTaxBtn" type="button" style="padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 13px; display:none;">Use my Simulator numbers</button>
        </div>
        <textarea id="r3expenses" placeholder="Paste your raw expenses here (e.g. 'Laptop $1200, Web hosting $150, Facebook ads $300') or use the buttons above — or leave blank and run this on your idea alone."></textarea>
      </div>
      <button class="primary" id="runTax"><span>Build projected Schedule C &amp; tax strategies</span></button>
      <div id="taxLoading" style="display:none;"></div>
      <div id="taxResult"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- LEARN TAB -->
    <div class="case-page round-page" id="round5" style="display:none;">
      <div class="round-label">Learn</div>
      <h2>Everything you need to know, in plain language</h2>
      <p class="dek">Written once with real sources baked in — IRS.gov, SBA.gov, and a few well-established explainer sites where a government source didn't cover it directly. Scroll through, or ask Claude anything not covered below.</p>

      <div id="faqList"></div>

      <div class="section-divider" style="margin:34px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"></div>

      <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin:0 0 6px;">Still have a question?</h3>
      <p class="dek">Ask Claude directly. Every answer cites a real source and shows the exact text it used — never a bare claim.</p>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="askClaudeBox">Your question <span id="askClaudeCounter" style="color:var(--ink-dim);font-weight:400;">(0/400)</span></label>
        <textarea id="askClaudeBox" maxlength="400" placeholder="e.g. 'What's the difference between a DBA and an LLC?'"></textarea>
      </div>
      <button class="primary" id="askClaudeBtn" type="button"><span>Ask Claude</span></button>
      <div id="askClaudeLoading" style="display:none;"></div>
      <div id="askClaudeResult"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="footer-row">
      <button class="ghost" id="exportBtn" style="display:none;">Save this file (.md)</button>
    </div>

    <div class="small-note">This is a reasoning tool, not licensed financial, legal, or tax advice — verify anything specific (deduction eligibility, filing thresholds, local regulations) with a CPA before you act on it.</div>

  </main>

  <!-- RIGHT RAIL: account, sticky -->
  <aside class="account-rail" id="accountRail">
    <div id="accountSignedIn" class="account-rail-inner" style="display:none;">
      <div class="account-profile">
        <div class="account-avatar" id="accountAvatar">?</div>
        <span class="account-email mono" id="accountEmail"></span>
      </div>
      <button class="ghost rail-btn" id="openSaved">My saved ideas</button>
      <button class="ghost rail-btn" id="saveToAccountBtn">Save this idea</button>
      <button class="ghost rail-btn" id="newIdeaBtn">+ New idea</button>
      <button class="ghost rail-btn" id="logoutBtn">Log out</button>
    </div>
    <div id="accountSignedOut" class="account-rail-inner" style="display:none;">
      <button class="ghost rail-btn" id="openLogin">Log in</button>
      <button class="ghost rail-btn" id="openSignup">Create account</button>
    </div>
  </aside>

</div><!-- /#appShell -->

<div class="modal-overlay" id="savedModal" style="display:none;">
  <div class="modal">
    <button class="modal-close" id="closeSavedModal" type="button">&times;</button>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:18px;">My saved ideas</h3>
    <div id="savedList"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="modal-overlay" id="deleteConfirmModal" style="display:none;z-index:200;">
  <div class="modal">
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:17px;">Delete this idea?</h3>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:14px;margin:0 0 18px;">This can't be undone.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;gap:8px;">
      <button class="ghost" id="cancelDeleteBtn" type="button">Cancel</button>
      <button class="primary" id="confirmDeleteBtn" type="button" style="background:var(--bad);border-color:var(--bad);"><span>Delete</span></button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="modal-overlay" id="newIdeaModal" style="display:none;">
  <div class="modal">
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:17px;">Start a new idea?</h3>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:14px;margin:0 0 18px;">You have unsaved work. Save it to your account first, or discard it and start fresh.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <button class="ghost" id="cancelNewIdeaBtn" type="button">Cancel</button>
      <button class="ghost" id="discardNewIdeaBtn" type="button">Discard &amp; start new</button>
      <button class="primary" id="saveThenNewIdeaBtn" type="button"><span>Save &amp; start new</span></button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="modal-overlay" id="cushionWizardModal" style="display:none;">
  <div class="modal" style="max-width:460px;">
    <button class="modal-close" id="cushionWizardCloseBtn" type="button">&times;</button>
    <div id="cushionWizardDots" style="display:flex;gap:6px;margin-bottom:16px;"></div>

    <!-- Step 1 -->
    <div class="wizard-step" id="cushionStep1">
      <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:17px;">How much do you have saved up?</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:13.5px;margin:0 0 16px;">Cash you could actually use to cover yourself — savings, not retirement accounts.</p>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="wizSavings">Current savings ($)</label>
        <input type="number" id="wizSavings" value="5000" min="0" step="100" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 2 -->
    <div class="wizard-step" id="cushionStep2" style="display:none;">
      <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:17px;">What do you spend per month, personally?</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:13.5px;margin:0 0 16px;">Rent, groceries, bills — your actual cost of living, not the business's expenses.</p>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="wizExpenses">Monthly personal expenses ($)</label>
        <input type="number" id="wizExpenses" value="2500" min="0" step="50" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 3 -->
    <div class="wizard-step" id="cushionStep3" style="display:none;">
      <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:17px;">Any loan or outside capital?</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:13.5px;margin:0 0 16px;">Leave at 0 if you're only using your own savings.</p>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="wizLoan">Loan / outside capital ($)</label>
        <input type="number" id="wizLoan" value="0" min="0" step="100" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 4 -->
    <div class="wizard-step" id="cushionStep4" style="display:none;">
      <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:17px;">How many hours a week can you commit?</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:13.5px;margin:0 0 16px;">This affects how realistic your ramp-up speed is — doesn't change the runway number itself.</p>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="wizHours">Hours/week</label>
        <input type="number" id="wizHours" value="20" min="0" max="168" step="1" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 5: result -->
    <div class="wizard-step" id="cushionStep5" style="display:none;">
      <h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:17px;">Here's your runway</h3>
      <div id="wizSummary" class="sim-summary" style="margin-bottom:14px;"></div>
      <div class="sim-chart-wrap" style="margin-bottom:14px;">
        <svg id="wizChart" viewBox="0 0 800 180" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"></svg>
      </div>
      <button class="primary" id="wizUseNumberBtn" type="button" style="width:100%;margin-bottom:10px;"><span>Use this number</span></button>
      <button class="ghost" id="wizAssessBtn" type="button" style="width:100%;margin-bottom:10px;">Get Claude's read on this</button>
      <div id="wizAssessLoading" style="display:none;"></div>
      <div id="wizAssessResult"></div>
    </div>

    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;margin-top:20px;">
      <button class="ghost" id="cushionWizBackBtn" type="button" style="visibility:hidden;">&larr; Back</button>
      <button class="primary" id="cushionWizNextBtn" type="button"><span>Next</span></button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="{{ url_for('static', filename='app.js') }}"></script>
</body>
</html>
